WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.498
Time of day strongly affects thermal patterns.

00:00:03.498 --> 00:00:09.877
Sunlight warms surfaces at different rates, and materials release stored heat differently after sunset.

00:00:09.877 --> 00:00:15.844
A warm roof area may reflect solar loading rather than an active defect.

00:00:15.844 --> 00:00:19.753
Wind cools surfaces and can reduce temperature differences.

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:26.132
Rain, fog, and humidity alter heat transfer and may reduce effective range or contrast.

00:00:26.132 --> 00:00:32.922
Water on a surface can change emissivity and create patterns unrelated to the suspected condition.

00:00:32.922 --> 00:00:37.655
Surface material, finish, angle, and texture affect emission and reflection.

00:00:37.655 --> 00:00:41.564
Shiny metal may reflect a nearby heat source.

00:00:41.564 --> 00:00:50.412
Glass may behave as a reflective or opaque surface in the thermal band rather than revealing what is behind it.

00:00:50.412 --> 00:00:55.144
Terrain and geometry create shadowing, exposure, drainage, and airflow differences.

00:00:55.144 --> 00:01:02.758
Seasonal vegetation, snow, soil moisture, and recent weather change the background against which an anomaly is judged.

00:01:02.758 --> 00:01:07.079
Environmental history matters, not only conditions at capture time.

00:01:07.079 --> 00:01:17.161
Recent sun, heating or cooling cycles, rain, equipment load, occupancy, and shutdown can determine whether a target has reached a useful thermal state.

00:01:17.161 --> 00:01:23.540
Interior and exterior temperature difference can also determine whether a building pattern is visible.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:32.799
If the thermal driving force is weak or changing rapidly, a negative result may simply mean the collection conditions were unsuitable.

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:39.589
Document temperature, wind, precipitation, humidity, sun, time, target state, distance, angle, and relevant recent conditions.

00:01:39.589 --> 00:01:46.791
If the environment cannot produce meaningful contrast, reschedule instead of forcing an interpretation from weak data.
